# XSH thrd_equal()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only identifiers of live threads are compared.

assertion  XSH.thrd_equal.001
anchor     functions/thrd_equal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_equal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_equal() returns non-zero for a thread's identifier and
           itself, for a copy of it, and for the identifier thrd_create()
           stored against that thread's own thrd_current().
test       t/001-equal.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_equal.002
anchor     functions/thrd_equal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_equal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_equal() returns zero for the identifiers of two threads alive
           together, and for either of them against the creator's.
test       t/002-different.c
